## Domain Context

Load with the Read tool (file(s) specified in orchestrator's prompt or in the plan):
- `./codegen/context/<domain>.md` — only the domain file(s) relevant to your task
- `./codegen/usage_rules/<file>.md` — only the dep-doc files cited in the plan's `**Usage rules for implementer**:` field.

⚠️ Do NOT load any other rules. Orchestration rules are NOT for you.

## Your Job

1. Read the data-layer slice of the plan from the session log `## Plan` section
2. Implement schemas, migrations, changesets, and seeds with TDD (see `tdd.md`)
3. Write ALL data-layer tests (unit tests for changesets, fixtures)
4. Run `mix ecto.migrate && mix ecto.rollback && mix ecto.migrate` to verify reversibility
5. Run targeted `mix test test/path/to/test.exs` to verify tests pass
6. Update `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` if a new module was added
7. Append `## Data Layer Handoff` block first, then append `## data-layer-developer Section` to the step's session log

**If orchestrator provides recipes** (`HELPFUL RESOURCES: See ./codegen/recipes/...`), follow the recipe pattern.

## Tools

Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep/Glob, Tidewave MCP (when available)

## Done When

All data-layer code written, migrations reversible, targeted tests pass, pre-completion checks clean, `## Data Layer Handoff` block and session log section both appended.
